<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<metadata>
  <!-- androidx.health.platform.client is connect-client's *internal* IPC/protobuf transport
       layer (Binder service stubs + a bundled protobuf-lite runtime) used to talk to the Health
       Platform service - not part of the public API surface this app calls. Whole categories of
       it fail to bind cleanly with class-parse: protobuf-lite's abstract generic Builder pattern
       (AbstractMessageLite.Builder.MergeFrom/Clone), and an AIDL-generated service-stub pattern
       (IHealthDataSdkService/HealthDataSdkService duplicate members/partial-class conflicts) -
       both well-known hard cases for Java/Kotlin binding tools generally, not something fixable
       from this project's own C# code. Excluding this whole internal package tree (rather than
       chasing individual classes within it one at a time, which was tried first and simply
       uncovered more of the same underlying problem) is safe: ScaleBridge only ever calls the
       public HealthConnectClient/WeightRecord/Mass/InsertRecordsResponse API surface, never
       anything under androidx.health.platform.client directly.

       androidx.health.connect.client.contracts holds ActivityResultContract-based classes for
       requesting exercise-route/health-permissions via Android's Activity Result APIs. This app
       requests permissions via plain runtime RequestPermissions (see MainActivity.cs) instead, so
       none of it is needed - and (like the internal package above) it has the same
       nullable-generic ActivityResultContract binding problem in more than one class here
       (ExerciseRouteRequestContract, HealthPermissionsRequestContract), so the whole package is
       excluded rather than each broken class individually.

       See docs/PROTOCOL_CONFIRMATION.md for the fuller explanation and iteration history, and
       what to check if a future connect-client version restructures these packages. -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[starts-with(@name, 'androidx.health.platform.client')]" />
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='androidx.health.connect.client.contracts']" />
</metadata>
